I understand that, and I wouldn't say the Wizard is a wimp or so.
The reason why I didn't *count* every move in his case is mostly
(I think) because of those repeatedly missing wands of death; at
some point they're empty, then I've to loot my bag to reorganize
and spend some more turns anyway. Or in case I have a cockatrice
in my bag stored recently I might save my wand of death charges
(which may miss anyway) to spend a turn to get that corpse. And
a third observation from my games; because of the missing wands
I try to position myself with a wall behind the Wizard so that
any zap has a double chance to hit; this may take one or more
turns. Therefore removing a wand from the bag I don't consider
a problem. Moreover, chances are low that a electric shock will
destroy a wand at that point in the game, so I also don't mind
to carry one in the open inventory.

>>My point was: "[...] But reflection is not necessary [...]"
