No, what I mean is some impression I got here from time to time
where folks full of paranoia claim that it's "impossible" or "a
pain" without it. My experience is that this is simply not true
in most games, and a nuisance in the remaining games.

> But on the whole, I wouldn't go beyond the castle without it.

Well, to each his own. Personally I completely avoid barracks or
Ludios if I have no reflection; chances are too high that soldiers
are equipped with wands. Gehennom, OTOH, with all those "twisty
passages" is quite safe, IME, but I admit there are also more
dangerous areas there, like the Sanctum and other open areas.

